# Local Data & Integrations

## Cloud source of truth (approved)

Coach business entities are stored in Supabase `public.coach_entities` with RLS
`user_id = auth.uid()`. Writes are **online-required** (no offline outbox in v1).
Drift `LocalEntities` is a **cache** (full replace per type after successful pull).

| Layer | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `CoachEntitiesRemote` | Supabase list/upsert/soft-delete/pull for coach entities |
| Feature `*Repository` classes | Feature APIs; remote-first writes, then update Drift cache |
| `OfflineLocalStore` | Drift cache for customers, plans, and related entities |
| `SharedPreferences` | Settings, drafts, exercise pins, PDF brand (not Postgres in v1) |
| `UserDataBackupService` | JSON disaster-recovery export/import; restore writes to remote + cache |
| `CloudBackupRepository` | Supabase Storage snapshots of the backup JSON (manual + automatic) |
| `CloudSnapshotScheduler` | Debounced automatic cloud snapshot uploads |
| `SyncOnOpenService` | Legacy snapshot merge helpers (entities pull is the live path) |

Always scope reads/writes by authenticated Supabase `userId`. Client uses **anon key + user JWT only** — never the service role.

```dart
// Writes: remote upsert/soft-delete first, then cache on success.
// Reads: prefer Drift cache; pull on login/resume and replace per type.
```

## Cloud backup snapshots (still allowed)

`CloudBackupRepository` may upload/list/download/delete the same JSON envelope
to the private `user-backups` bucket. This remains disaster recovery alongside
live `coach_entities` CRUD. See `docs/sync-strategy.md`.

## Do not add

- GymBlog.API client or `GYMBLOG_API_URL` wiring
- Offline outbox / `SyncOrchestrator` remote replay without a new approved plan
- Service-role keys in the Flutter app or bundled assets
- Third-party workout app integrations (e.g. Hevy) without an approved plan
- Sharing entities across coaches (RLS is per-owner only)

## Agent deny-list (do not reintroduce without approved plan)

- `lib/core/network/gymblog_api_client.dart` or any GymBlog HTTP client
- `GYMBLOG_API_URL` in env, CI secrets, or bundled assets
- `SyncOrchestrator` remote replay wired in `main.dart` bootstrap
- `get_it` or a global DI container
- Remote write paths via `PendingOperations` expecting server ACK
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE` (or any service-role secret) in the Flutter client
- `lib/features/integrations/hevy/` or a `dio`-based Hevy (or similar) client
